Browser : (http://google.com) or http://localhost.

DNS Lookup : The system queries DNS to map the domain name to an IP address

IP Address : The browser gets the target destination IP address.

TCP Connection : A reliable connection is established with the server (via a 3-way handshake).

Port 80/443 : Traffic reaches the target port (80 for HTTP or 443 for HTTPS).

Web Server : A process like Nginx handles the request

HTTP Response : The server returns status codes (200 OK), headers, and the response body.

